Here are 3 real-life examples where an infinite while loop is used:

1. ATM Machine
An ATM keeps running continuously to serve users.
It only stops when the system is shut down.
while (true) {
    // Wait for user to insert card
    // Process transactions
}
2. Game Loop (Video Games)
Games keep running until the player exits.
The screen keeps updating, taking input, and rendering graphics.
while (true) {
    // Take user input
    // Update game state
    // Display output
}
3. Server Listening for Requests
A web server runs continuously, waiting for client requests.
while (true) {
    // Listen for client request
    // Process request
    // Send response
}
